{"case_id":"C006","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":98,"change_types":["bug_fix","HTTP/1 chunked-framing correction"],"affected_functions":["on_send_request"],"reason":"The commit only corrects the terminating chunk emitted by the existing HTTP/1 client path from \"0\\r\\n\" to the protocol-complete \"0\\r\\n\\r\\n\". It introduces no new entry point, API requirement, initialization, configuration, state requirement, or input constraint. The existing driver already configures a reverse proxy and supplies fuzz-controlled requests through the normal HTTP server path, so this localized output-framing fix does not make the harness inadequate.","evidence":["In lib/common/http1client.c, on_send_request changes only the literal used when client->_is_chunked is true.","The function still clears client->_is_chunked, updates bytes_written, and calls h2o_socket_write through the same control flow and API.","fuzz/driver.cc already registers /reproxy-test with h2o_proxy_register_reverse_proxy and feeds arbitrary input into h2o_http1_accept or h2o_http2_accept.","No production interfaces, configuration fields, initialization steps, or accepted-input conditions are added or changed."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing fuzz harness unchanged; no maintenance is required for this protocol-framing bug fix."}
